          "2": "# The Damingos Band Interview Newspaper 1974\n[[](https://www.instagram.com/phoebestreetlive) phoebestreetlive 2,763 Phoebe St. LIVE is a new show recorded and shot @phoebestreetstudio in Toronto to document and further humanize the beauty and power of music. Raw, unfiltered and LIVE. We use a mix of vintage and new high-grade analog recording equipment to both record and mix the audio and a film crew of industry professionals use an equally powerful combination of cameras and lights to capture the visual part of the performance in a cinematic and engaging way. Episode four features up-and-coming Montreal garage rock duo, THE FLAMINGOS PINK. A band you might have caught on tour in Canada while they were out supporting their most recent release ‘GROWF’. A hooky, well-crafted EP that captures their sense of humour, passion and range. Acoustic-heavy and tongue-in-cheek track ‘Change Your Ways’ is an instant classic. I had the good fortune of being trusted with producing the songs for that recording at Phoebe St. Studio and I can tell you that those two guys put a lot of love and care into bringing them to life. And they dealt with each other in such a positive, constructive and respectful way while navigating the forever part of the process. It was inspiring. Their Phoebe St. LIVE set is some rock and roll catharsis driven by powerhouse vocals from guitarist Sacha Gubany while “off-the-wall” drummer and backing vocalist Julien Corrado drops a bass drum of death to bring the low end. An earnest and raucous performance in keeping with the spirit of the show. Enjoy! Peace, love and live music, Rob Higgins (executive producer / host) @riverherbertjoggins director/editor : JR Reid, Hands Editorial dop : Alex Chung sound engineer : Rob Sanzo mixing : Rob Higgins, Rob Sanzo lighting : John Pogue colourist : Darrin Klimek, Accomplice Post Support provided by INTECH Risk Management and Spy Cider House and Distillery. Proud, community-minded supporters of independent artists and makers.",
